        muxctrl_reg1 and muxctrl_reg2 are group registers: one 2-bit field switches nine pads (the VIU0 or VIU1 clock and data pads) at once between the pad's own VIU function, GPIO, FE PHY debug and the next pad's VIU function (data sheet 2.4, Tables 2-31 to 2-33).

        Pad drive-strength and pull controls are in the separate pad control registers of the same description (not repeated here).

        ### Power, reset and system modes (data sheet 3.1, 3.2.3, 3.9)

        * Resets: global hard reset npor from the RSTN pin (the low pulse must last more than 12 XIN cycles and XIN must be stable); global soft reset sys_rst_n from the system controller (resets everything except the clock/reset circuits and test logic; at least 360 system clock cycles until release); per-module soft resets xx_rst_n from the PERI_CRG control registers. A module soft reset is not released automatically: write 1 to reset, 0 to release. Diagram: reset tree.
        * System modes (SYS_CTRL): NORMAL (24 MHz crystal, 46.875 kHz clock and APLL enabled: the ARM subsystem runs from the PLL), SLOW (APLL off: the ARM subsystem runs from the 24 MHz crystal), DOZE (APLL off: the ARM subsystem runs from the 46.875 kHz clock divided from the crystal). The A9/DDR/bus clock is the crystal clock after power-on.
        * Module power controls: USB 2.0 host (PERI_CRG46 bit 7 = 0 stops the clock, PERIPHCTRL21 bit 22 = 1 powers the USB PHY down), SATA (PERI_CRG45 bits 9/8 = 0 stop port 0/1, PERIPHCTRL25 bit 2 = 1 powers the SATA PHY down), video DACs (PERI_CRG13 bits 7/6 = 0 stop the SD/HD DAC clocks, PERIPHCTRL4 bits 30/31 = 1 power the SD/HD DAC down), PLLs (PERI_CRG1 bit 21 / CRG3 bit 21 / CRG9 bit 21 = 0 power APLL / VPLL0 / EPLL down), BOOTROM ROM power (PERIPHCTRL2 bit 0 = 1). DDR: self-refresh through DDRC_SREFCTRL.sr_seq.
        * PLL change sequence: switch the A9/DDR/bus to the crystal first, change the PLL configuration (PLL stable after 0.1 ms; wait time in SC_PLLCTRL[27:3]), then switch back.
        * Chip clock domains are described under the clock tree diagram; the data sheet has no separate power-domain (island) table.

